N1  - <p>BOINC criterion evidence - Abstract, verbatim: "A fault tolerant and asynchronous implementation of Gibbs sampling using the Berkeley Open Infrastructure for Network Computing (BOINC) was used to identify the location of binding sites of the SNAI1 (Snail) and SNAI2 (Slug) transcription factors across the human genome." Introduction, verbatim: "This paper presents new results from DNA@Home [1], which uses BOINC [2] to provide massively scalable computing power to search for transcription factor binding sites (or motifs) in large datasets." Also: "Utilizing over 1500 volunteer computing hosts for a period of two months, 18 different parallel Gibbs sampling runs were performed..." | Full text: IEEE e-Science 2015, DOI 10.1109/eScience.2015.27 | Link: DNA@Home / BOINC | Source: IEEE e-Science (2015)ER&nbsp;&nbsp;-</p>
